# Learnings

Accumulated knowledge from Forge sessions. Updated automatically at session end.

<!-- Append new learnings below this line -->

## 2026-07-19 — Runtime 2.0 boundary

- Host enhancement is independently packaged as `forge-runtime`; installation must never import
  from a source checkout.
- Codex, Claude Code, and Cursor share one governed 106-skill catalog while retaining native
  discovery and configuration contracts.
- Runtime MCP tools are read-only. Autonomous planning and execution belong to Praxis and must not
  be reintroduced through compatibility shims.
- Installer, update, pack removal, rollback, and uninstall paths preserve user-owned configuration
  and historical state by default.

## 2026-07-20 — RAT-Image evidence review (revision 1205445f)

- `docs/harness_engineering_analysis.md`: harness quality is bounded by evaluator quality; weak or
  fuzzy evaluators are the first bottleneck before context, memory, or workflow search. Forge keeps
  activation and outcome evals as the primary guardrails and treats negative results as recordable
  evidence, not noise.
- `docs/robotics_frameworks_survey.md`: compose mature designs instead of forking a monorepo;
  dataset schema versions are breaking contracts; support tiers must state what is reliable rather
  than claiming every combination works. Candidate follow-up: an `imitation-learning` upgrade pass
  from the LeRobot v0.6 policy-zoo and dataset-v3 analysis.
- `docs/mw_training.md`: environment-suite commit pinning and fixed checkpoint-export schedules are
  load-bearing for reproducible RL victim training; absorbed into `rl-training` source map.

